# Electric reference update — 2026-10-29

The Electric model already had a recent silver fastback rebuild with the slim light bar, recessed front curtains, sculpted sides and fitted mirrors described in `VOLT_NEW_REFERENCES_2026_10_29.md`. This follow-up narrows the painted band above the rear glass and changes the five aero wheel faces to broader, nearly radial satin graphite blades. The existing painted rear pillars, saved liveries, wheel articulation and handling remain intact. An attempted roof change was discarded after a native preview showed an uneven edge.

The procedural preview is recorded in [side](evidence/electric-reference-update-2026-10-29/side-clean.png), [front quarter](evidence/electric-reference-update-2026-10-29/front-quarter-clean.png) and [rear quarter](evidence/electric-reference-update-2026-10-29/rear-quarter-clean.png) views. The v24 prepared meshes, five racing shadows, Electric Garage template, header and Garage pictures, 49 livery previews and news picture were regenerated using the existing Godot bake scripts.

Focused checks passed: reference body 25/25, window refinement 18/18, racing model 23/23, native model 34/34 and actual App 58/58. The unchanged cabin fixture reports 44/46: its two lower rear-glass bound failures also occur with the archived v23 mesh (maximum Z 1.8260865 against a 1.82 limit). The adjusted mesh matches that bound within floating-point precision. The full detailed model remains 118,714 triangles, with 38,324 visible simple triangles and 3,671 shadow triangles. Desktop App hitch messages occurred during the integration run.

Godot was run with isolated local profiles; sandboxed attempts encountered Windows certificate-store access errors, and the successful bakes and checks used normal access. Existing appearance saves and handling resources were not modified. Reloading/reimporting the project and visual acceptance on the owner's device remain.
